                <pb facs="0523" n="478" xml:id="pg478"/>

                <head>168. Memorandum From Director of Central Intelligence Turner to President Carter, Vice President Mondale, Secretary of State Vance, Secretary of Defense Brown, and the President’s Assistant for
                    National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d168-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1980-01-15">January 15, 1980</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The attached paper sets forth our preliminary views of Soviet options and
                    constraints in Southwest Asia following the invasion of Afghanistan. Its focus
                    is on the major actors in the region from the Soviet perspective; it does not
                    deal explicitly with possible US policies or how those might influence Soviet
                    positions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">Stansfield
                                Turner</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d168-f2"/></signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d168-a1.xml" xpointer="d168-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
